304
00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:25.420
We reached out to writer Aaron Schur, the writer of this episode, because we were very curious who wrote,
我们联系了本集的编剧亚伦·舒尔，因为我们非常好奇是谁写了那句台词，

305
00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:27.780
Tastes Like Splenda Gets You Drunk Like Scotch.
“喝起来像代糖，醉起来像威士忌”。

306
00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:28.740
Yeah, we gotta know.
是啊，我们一定要知道。

307
00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:30.400
I mean, it's just too good.
我是说，这台词太棒了。

308
00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:37.180
And he said that that line was created in a pre-table draft pitch session.
他说那句台词是在剧本围读前的头脑风暴会上创作出来的。

309
00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:44.680
So what that means is the writers, they would kind of typically work together to make an outline of each episode.
意思就是编剧们通常会一起工作，为每一集列出一个大纲。

310
00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:50.940
And then a specific writer, in this case, Aaron Schur, would go off and write the whole episode based on that outline.
然后由特定的编剧，在这个案例中就是亚伦·舒尔，根据大纲去完成整集的剧本。

311
00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:52.860
And they usually got, like, about a week.
他们通常有一周左右的时间。

312
00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:59.840
Well, they would turn in their draft, they would get notes, and then they would also have these pitch sessions.
他们会提交初稿，收到修改意见，然后还会进行头脑风暴会议。

313
00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:00.660
Right.
对。

314
00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:01.300
They'll get notes.
他们会收到修改意见。

315
00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:06.160
Sometimes a few of the writers will be put in a pod to pitch on a certain element of the script.
有时几位编剧会被分成小组，专门针对剧本的某个部分进行头脑风暴。

316
00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:09.220
Yes, and that is exactly what happened with Scotch and Splenda.
没错，这就是“苏格兰威士忌加代糖”这个梗的由来。

317
00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:18.100
A few writers got together, and they said, we want a really funny joke for this moment when Michael is walking around with a drink in his hand.
几位编剧聚在一起，说他们想为迈克尔手里拿着酒走来走去的那个瞬间设计一个特别好笑的梗。

318
00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:23.180
And Aaron had saved all of the pitches.
而亚伦保存了所有的备选方案。

319
00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:24.200
Stop it.
别卖关子了。

320
00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:25.280
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

321
00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:26.780
All of the, oh, my gosh.
所有的，天哪。

322
00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:28.160
What, what, what were they?
是什么，是什么，都是些什么？

323
00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:32.460
Okay, so, Kevin says, is that Scotch?
好吧，凯文问：“那是苏格兰威士忌吗？”

324
00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:32.820
Yeah.
对。

325
00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:36.860
And here are the various pitches that Michael would reply.
以下是迈克尔回答的各种备选方案。

326
00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:40.480
Yup, from a firetruck-shaped bottle in my office.
“没错，是从我办公室里那个消防车形状的瓶子里倒出来的。”

327
00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:44.220
Or, better, Southern Comfort.
或者更好一点的，“是南部舒适力娇酒”。

328
00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:49.840
Or, nope, Diet Pepsi and water and ice and Scotch.
或者，“不，是健怡百事可乐加水加冰块再加苏格兰威士忌”。

329
00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:53.520
Or, it's non-alcoholic Scotch.
或者，“这是无酒精苏格兰威士忌”。

330
00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:57.880
And finally, the one they went with, Scotch and Splenda.
最后，他们选用了那句：苏格兰威士忌加代糖。

331
00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:00.900
Tastes like Splenda, gets you drunk like Scotch.
“喝起来像代糖，醉起来像威士忌”。

332
00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:10.440
And then that is the joke that they ultimately picked for our table read draft, which is the draft that all the actors got and that we would read out loud.
这就是他们最终选定放入围读剧本里的梗，也就是演员们拿到手并大声朗读的那个版本。

333
00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:11.680
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

334
00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:14.940
My number two would have been a bottle shaped like a firetruck.
我心里的第二名是那个消防车形状的瓶子。

335
00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.160
I liked bottle shaped like a firetruck as well.
我也挺喜欢消防车形状的瓶子。

336
00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:23.240
Because I remember, like, my dad had, like, a novelty liqueur that, I think it came in a stagecoach.
因为我记得我爸爸以前有一种新奇的力娇酒，我记得它是装在一个驿站马车形状的瓶子里的。

337
00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:23.960
Which, I don't know.
这我就不知道了。

338
00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:25.500
But, like, it just sat on the shelf.
但它就一直摆在架子上。

339
00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:30.540
Well, the cool thing about those extra lines was, then at the table draft, if a...
嗯，这些额外台词最酷的地方在于，在围读剧本时，如果……

340
00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:33.460
Oh, Angela is having a sip of Scotch and Splenda.
哦，安吉拉正在喝苏格兰威士忌加代糖。

341
00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:34.580
That's the ice that you hear.
你听到的那是冰块的声音。

342
00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:37.260
Because I was like, well, we are talking about Scotch and Splenda.
因为我当时想，既然我们在聊苏格兰威士忌加代糖。

343
00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:39.980
It wasn't a joke, folks.
大家伙儿，这可不是开玩笑。

344
00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:41.060
We're really drinking it.
我们是真的在喝。

345
00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:42.240
Sipping.
小口抿着。

346
00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:43.060
Sipping it.
抿着喝。

347
00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:43.940
We're really sipping it.
我们是真的在抿着喝。

348
00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:44.860
That's true, you are sipping.
没错，你确实在抿着喝。

349
00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:54.620
But what I was going to say is, the interesting thing is that those extra jokes, the ones they didn't put in the table draft, they would save in that candy bag document.
但我刚才想说的是，有趣的地方在于，那些没被放进围读剧本的额外笑话，他们会把它们存进那个“糖果袋”文档里。

350
00:14:54.860 --> 00:15:02.300
And then if a joke didn't land at the table read, they might go over there and replace it when it came time for the shooting draft.
然后如果某个笑话在围读时效果不好，他们可能会去那里找个备选，在定稿拍摄时替换掉它。

351
00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.600
Or they would have us do it on set.
或者他们会让我们在片场拍。

352
00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:04.900
Right.
没错。

353
00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:05.820
All the different alternates.
所有不同的备选台词。

354
00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:06.180
Right.
没错。

355
00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:09.140
Sometimes I think the writers just wanted to hear them, just for fun.
有时候我觉得编剧只是想听听看，纯粹为了好玩。

356
00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:15.020
Even though they knew we weren't going to, like, use any of them, they would hand you a page, and if we had time that day in our shooting schedule,
即使他们知道我们可能根本不会用，他们还是会给你一张纸，如果那天拍摄进度有空档的话，

357
00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:16.700
we would just do a whole bunch of alts.
我们就会把那一堆备选台词都演一遍。

358
00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:18.060
And it was always so fun.
而且总是特别有意思。

359
00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:18.580
So fun.
特别有意思。

360
00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:21.840
Stanley thinks Michael should start looking for another job.
斯坦利认为迈克尔应该开始找下一份工作了。

361
00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:27.140
Michael says he has a job, to which Andy points out for four more days.
迈克尔说他有工作，安迪指出他只剩四天了。

362
00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:27.520
Yeah.
是啊。

363
00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:29.880
Andy's like, you kind of got to get your act together here.
安迪的意思是，你得振作起来了。

364
00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:33.400
Well, Michael has a talking head where he is not worried.
嗯，迈克尔有个采访镜头，他说他一点也不担心。

365
00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.020
I mean, what's he going to do?
我是说，他能做什么呢？

366
00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:39.000
He's going to do a little bit of this, a little bit of that, and he's going to stop worrying about calories.
他会做点这个，做点那个，而且他打算不再去管卡路里了。

367
00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:46.920
So during this whole montage of, like, people giving Michael advice, there was a scene in the shooting draft that didn't make it.
所以在这一整段大家给迈克尔提建议的蒙太奇里，剧本初稿里有个场景没被剪进去。

368
00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:50.740
And Kelly walks into his office, and she's like, Michael, what are you going to do?
凯莉走进他的办公室说，迈克尔，你打算怎么办？

369
00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:51.800
You know what I would do?
你知道我会怎么做吗？

370
00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:52.760
I'd move to Mexico.
我会搬到墨西哥去。

371
00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:53.740
I'd live on the beach.
我会住在海滩上。

372
00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:54.620
I'd be naked.
我会赤身裸体。

373
00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:58.620
I'd make jewelry, have amazing sex, drink lots of margaritas.
我会做首饰，享受美妙的性生活，喝很多玛格丽特酒。

374
00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:01.240
She just kind of goes off on this whole thing.
她就那样滔滔不绝地说了一大通。

375
00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:10.060
And while Kelly is rambling on and on about what she would do, he is carving into his desk, Michael was here.
当凯莉在那儿喋喋不休地说她会做什么时，迈克尔正在桌子上刻字，“迈克尔到此一游”。

376
00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:11.800
Oh, my God.
天哪。

377
00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:14.080
And he really carved into the top of the desk.
而且他是真的刻在了桌面上。

378
00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:19.480
I was like, did we trash a desk for this, like, scene that never even made it in?
我当时就在想，我们为了这个甚至没被剪进正片的场景，真的毁掉了一张桌子吗？

379
00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.380
And I wasn't the only one that noticed.
而且注意到这一点的不仅是我。

380
00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:22.380
Olivia C.
奥利维亚·C。

381
00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:26.160
wrote in and said, in the deleted scenes, they're on the DVD box set, guys.
写信来说，伙计们，这些都在DVD套装的删减片段里。

382
00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:28.280
We see that Michael has carved.
我们看到迈克尔刻了字。

383
00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:29.660
Michael was here on the desk.
桌上有“迈克尔到此一游”。

384
00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:32.240
Did Steve really carve that into the desk?
史蒂夫是真的把字刻在桌子上了吗？

385
00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:34.200
Olivia, I had the same question.
奥利维亚，我也有同样的疑问。

386
00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:34.800
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

387
00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.220
Randy Cordray had the answer.
兰迪·科德雷有答案。

388
00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:43.980
He said our production designer, Michael Gallenberg, created a matching desktop out of the exact same similar wood.
他说我们的美术指导迈克尔·加伦伯格用完全相同的木材制作了一个配套的桌面。

389
00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:44.560
Wow.
哇。

390
00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:45.340
I know.
我知道。

391
00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:50.800
That was laminated over the actual desktop because we were shooting scenes out of order,
那是贴在真实桌面上的贴面，因为我们拍摄场景的顺序是乱的，

392
00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:57.160
and they couldn't have different stages of Michael carving into his desk in the episode because then it wouldn't match.
他们不能让迈克尔在剧集中出现不同程度的刻字，否则画面就对不上了。

393
00:16:57.420 --> 00:16:57.680
Yeah.
没错。

394
00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:01.040
So they just had this laminate top they would put on top, and then they would take it away.
所以他们只是准备了这个可以放上去又可以拿下来的贴面。

395
00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:02.940
Now, let me ask you this question.
现在，让我问你一个问题。

396
00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:03.280
Okay.
好的。

397
00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:12.460
That means that Veda, our script supervisor, would have had a chart, and on that chart, for each scene, it would say carve desk, no carve desk.
这意味着我们的场记维达会有一张表，表上会针对每一场戏标注“刻桌子”或“不刻桌子”。

398
00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:15.420
She would have tracked when we should see the carving.
她得追踪我们什么时候该看到刻痕。

399
00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:16.060
Yes.
是的。

400
00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:19.800
But they didn't know they were going to cut this scene until later.
但他们当时并不知道后来会把这个场景剪掉。

401
00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:20.420
Right.
没错。

402
00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:26.120
So is it possible that we can see this carving on his desk throughout the episode?
那么我们有可能在这一集中一直看到他桌上的这个雕刻吗？

403
00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:27.160
Maybe.
也许吧。

404
00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:28.720
You'd have to be close, right?
你得离得很近才行，对吧？

405
00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:29.680
Like over his shoulder.
就像站在他肩膀后面那样。

406
00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:30.200
Yeah.
是啊。

407
00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:36.760
But, I mean, probably what a headache for Veda, like keeping track of all that, and then it didn't even make it in.
但我的意思是，这对维达来说得多头疼啊，要追踪所有这些细节，结果最后还没用上。

408
00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:42.500
I'll have you know, Angela, at 2 minutes 48 seconds, we had a fan catch from Flora K.
安吉拉，我得告诉你，在2分48秒的时候，有位粉丝弗洛拉·K发现了它。

409
00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:47.500
There is a blooming plant at reception.
接待处有一盆正在开花的植物。

410
00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:48.680
Flora?
弗洛拉？

411
00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:49.860
Good catch.
发现得好。

412
00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:51.660
I knew it would make your heart happy, Angela.
我就知道这会让你开心的，安吉拉。

413
00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:52.560
I saw it too, Flora.
我也看到了，弗洛拉。

414
00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:56.800
You know, the last time we had a blooming plant at reception was beach games.
你知道吗，我们上一次在接待处看到开花的植物还是在海滩游戏那一集。

415
00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:59.440
So you think this is connected to Pam?
所以你认为这和帕姆有关？

416
00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:01.020
Pam is going to have her moment here.
帕姆在这里会有属于她的高光时刻。

417
00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:02.660
She's going to have another moment.
她会有另一个高光时刻。

418
00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:05.820
She's going to bloom again today, like in beach games.
她今天会再次绽放，就像在海滩游戏里那样。

419
00:18:05.820 --> 00:18:12.800
Now, I know we talked to Steve Ducharer, who told us that it was a coincidence, that it was a blooming plant for beach games.
我知道我们和史蒂夫·杜查雷聊过，他告诉我们那只是个巧合，海滩游戏里的那盆花只是刚好开了。

420
00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:18.260
But Steve Ducharer, again, with the blooming plant, Pam is blooming.
但史蒂夫·杜查雷，又是那盆开花的植物，帕姆正在绽放。

421
00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:19.620
I think it was subconscious.
我觉得那是潜意识的。

422
00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:21.140
This is that group mind thing.
这就是所谓的集体潜意识。

423
00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:21.860
That's what I was going to say.
我正想说这个。

424
00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:23.140
This is creative group mind.
这就是创作上的集体潜意识。

425
00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:26.700
Well, Michael is now going to move into the kitchen.
好了，迈克尔现在要走进厨房了。

426
00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:29.880
I guess he's hungry, so he's looking for some food.
我猜他饿了，所以想找点吃的。

427
00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:34.240
He's a little tipsy, and he's going to go, like, raid the refrigerator.
他有点醉醺醺的，打算去洗劫冰箱。

428
00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:35.460
Who hasn't been there?
谁没经历过这种时候呢？

429
00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:35.980
Come on.
得了吧。

430
00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:42.200
In the script, it just said that Michael takes out a container clearly labeled Phyllis.
剧本里只写了迈克尔拿出一个明确贴着“菲利斯”标签的容器。

431
00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:45.540
But you know how he's eating it, and then he's like, ugh, Phyllis.
但你知道他是怎么吃的，吃完之后他说，呃，菲利斯。

432
00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:46.900
None of that was in the script.
这些剧本里都没有。

433
00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:48.320
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

434
00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:48.920
Nope.
没有。

435
00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:50.220
Steve just improvised that.
那是史蒂夫即兴发挥的。

436
00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:51.820
Oh, that's so good.
哦，那太棒了。

437
00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:56.480
Andy comes in, and he wants to give Michael some wine as a farewell gift.
安迪进来了，他想送迈克尔一些酒作为告别礼物。

438
00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.840
It's actually a really nice gesture.
这其实是一个非常好的举动。

439
00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.060
It is.
确实。

440
00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:02.600
And Michael just doesn't give a crap.
但迈克尔根本不在乎。

441
00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:06.160
Michael would love it if Jim came in and gave him a bottle of wine.
如果吉姆进来送他一瓶酒，迈克尔肯定会很高兴的。

442
00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:06.960
I know.
我知道。

443
00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:11.580
But, you know, it's Andy, so he's like, ugh, I already have wine.
但你知道，那是安迪，所以他就像是，呃，我已经有酒了。

444
00:19:11.780 --> 00:19:16.080
This next scene I loved because Michael's sitting on the couch by front reception,
接下来的这个场景我很喜欢，因为迈克尔坐在前台旁边的沙发上，

445
00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:17.720
and a man walks in.
然后一个男人走了进来。

446
00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:20.800
He's interviewing for Michael's job.
他来面试迈克尔的职位。

447
00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:24.180
Yeah, Michael is kind of on the couch reading a novel.
是的，迈克尔当时正坐在沙发上看小说。

448
00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:25.700
I zoomed in on it.
我把画面放大了。

449
00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:27.300
I tried to see what it was.
我试着看清那是什么书。

450
00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:29.580
It's like a woman in a martini glass.
看起来像是一个坐在马提尼酒杯里的女人。

451
00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:32.320
It's clearly like a sort of-
这看起来显然像是一种……

452
00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:32.920
A romance novel?
言情小说吗？

453
00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:39.020
No, it seems like one of those, like, books for women about, you know, claim your space
不，看起来像是那种，你知道的，写给女性看的，关于“主宰你的空间”之类的书。

454
00:19:39.020 --> 00:19:41.020
sort of book.
那样的书。

455
00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:41.520
Yeah, yeah.
对，没错。

456
00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:42.640
Like a motivational-
就像那种励志……

457
00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:43.200
Yes.
是的。

458
00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:44.800
That's what it looked like to me.
我看起来也是那样。

459
00:19:45.340 --> 00:19:47.220
I want you to know a couple of things.
有几件事我想让你知道。

460
00:19:47.440 --> 00:19:51.020
At 4 minutes, 16 seconds, the blooming plant is on the move.
在4分16秒时，那盆花换位置了。

461
00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:53.840
It's been moved to the other side of the reception desk.
它被移到了接待台的另一边。

462
00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:55.260
So you can see the couch better.
