00:40:19.110 --> 00:40:19.590
Excuse me.
打扰一下。

944
00:40:22.870 --> 00:40:23.470
Hello.
你好。

945
00:40:23.850 --> 00:40:24.210
Hey.
嘿。

946
00:40:25.010 --> 00:40:26.750
Having a nice stay here?
在这里住得还习惯吗？

947
00:40:27.930 --> 00:40:28.530
Great.
很好。

948
00:40:30.810 --> 00:40:32.430
You must be from Jamba Juice.
你一定是来自果汁工坊吧。

949
00:40:33.690 --> 00:40:35.110
Uh, what's that?
呃，那是什么？

950
00:40:35.890 --> 00:40:37.930
It's a juice company because you're a smoothie.
那是一家果汁公司，因为你是个“冰沙”（smoothie，双关语，意指油嘴滑舌的人）。

951
00:40:39.110 --> 00:40:39.710
Okay.
好吧。

952
00:40:41.130 --> 00:40:41.970
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

953
00:40:42.270 --> 00:40:42.850
Sorry about that.
对此我很抱歉。

954
00:40:49.100 --> 00:40:50.500
Up, shut up, shut up.
闭嘴，闭嘴，闭嘴。

955
00:40:51.060 --> 00:40:56.280
So she has this really lame pickup line and then immediately just hates herself and goes
她用了个特别烂的搭讪台词，然后立刻就开始厌恶自己，跑去

956
00:40:56.280 --> 00:40:58.380
in the corner and is like, why did I do that?
角落里想，我为什么要那样做？

957
00:40:58.800 --> 00:41:03.320
Well, this leads us into a scene that I will call awkward in the kitchen.
好吧，这把我们带入了一个我称之为“厨房尴尬”的场景。

958
00:41:03.720 --> 00:41:05.520
Oh, so awkward.
哦，太尴尬了。

959
00:41:06.240 --> 00:41:08.940
Michael is still trying to recruit people for his business.
迈克尔还在试图招募人手加入他的公司。

960
00:41:09.240 --> 00:41:12.980
And Andy does that thing, you know, that people do when they're uncomfortable.
安迪做了那件事，你知道的，人们在感到不自在时会做的事。

961
00:41:12.980 --> 00:41:15.560
They either sing their answer or they do an accent.
他们要么把回答唱出来，要么就模仿口音。

962
00:41:15.560 --> 00:41:17.160
I think I'm the accent person.
我觉得我是那种会模仿口音的人。

963
00:41:17.520 --> 00:41:18.640
I sing stuff.
我会把事情唱出来。

964
00:41:18.640 --> 00:41:21.700
Yeah, when you don't want to, like, really tip your hand.
是啊，当你不想真正表露意图的时候。

965
00:41:21.940 --> 00:41:22.240
Yeah.
是啊。

966
00:41:22.920 --> 00:41:25.460
So Andy's like, oh, oh, interesting idea.
所以安迪就说，哦，哦，有意思的想法。

967
00:41:25.740 --> 00:41:27.420
Like, he does some ridiculous accent.
就像他用那种荒谬的口音说话一样。

968
00:41:27.560 --> 00:41:30.200
But you would be like, that's a very interesting offer.
但你会说，那真是个非常有趣的提议。

969
00:41:31.120 --> 00:41:31.520
Yeah.
是啊。

970
00:41:31.740 --> 00:41:34.780
I mean, the other day I did it while we were working together.
我是说，前几天我们一起工作的时候我就这样做了。

971
00:41:35.120 --> 00:41:36.860
When we were working on that document.
当我们处理那份文档的时候。

972
00:41:37.100 --> 00:41:37.620
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

973
00:41:37.780 --> 00:41:41.580
I was like, this PDF editing is difficult.
我说，编辑这个PDF太难了。

974
00:41:42.020 --> 00:41:43.440
And then I was like, are you okay?
然后我就问，你还好吗？

975
00:41:43.600 --> 00:41:45.600
Because it sounds like you're about to spiral.
因为听起来你快要崩溃了。

976
00:41:46.020 --> 00:41:47.180
I was like, yeah.
我说，是啊。

977
00:41:48.840 --> 00:41:51.980
Well, it gets only more cringy because now Dwight comes in.
好吧，这只会变得更尴尬，因为现在德怀特进来了。

978
00:41:52.100 --> 00:41:55.540
But Michael does not ask Dwight to join his company.
但迈克尔并没有邀请德怀特加入他的公司。

979
00:41:55.540 --> 00:41:59.120
But it is also clear that Dwight wouldn't say yes anyway.
但也很明显，反正德怀特也不会答应。

980
00:41:59.400 --> 00:41:59.700
Yeah.
是啊。

981
00:41:59.700 --> 00:42:01.580
So he's like, I've got the farm and a thing.
所以他说，我有农场还有别的事要忙。

982
00:42:01.720 --> 00:42:02.640
And let's put a pin in it.
咱们先把这事搁置一下吧。

983
00:42:02.700 --> 00:42:04.220
Yeah, let's definitely put a pin in that.
是啊，绝对得先把这事搁置一下。

984
00:42:05.380 --> 00:42:05.840
Yeah.
是啊。

985
00:42:06.220 --> 00:42:09.460
Well, we got a lot of mail about this kitchen scene.
嗯，我们收到了很多关于这个厨房场景的邮件。

986
00:42:09.460 --> 00:42:17.500
A lot of people felt like it was out of character for Dwight to not want to join Michael's paper company.
很多人觉得德怀特不想加入迈克尔的造纸公司不符合他的人设。

987
00:42:18.100 --> 00:42:22.440
And also, people wondered, why didn't Michael want him to join?
而且，人们还纳闷，为什么迈克尔不想让他加入？

988
00:42:22.480 --> 00:42:24.600
And I just didn't know if we wanted to discuss.
我只是不知道我们是否想讨论这个。

989
00:42:24.600 --> 00:42:26.400
I have my thoughts.
我有我的想法。

990
00:42:26.720 --> 00:42:27.820
Let me hear them.
说来听听。

991
00:42:28.280 --> 00:42:29.680
Dwight is a survivaliSt.
德怀特是个生存主义者。

992
00:42:30.020 --> 00:42:33.480
And he doesn't think Michael's company is going to survive.
他不认为迈克尔的公司能活下去。

993
00:42:34.880 --> 00:42:41.720
So ultimately, even though he loves Michael, he's not going to go somewhere where he won't survive, right?
所以归根结底，尽管他爱迈克尔，但他不会去一个他无法生存的地方，对吧？

994
00:42:41.940 --> 00:42:42.160
Yeah.
是啊。

995
00:42:42.160 --> 00:42:44.600
So I think he's very practical.
所以我认为他非常务实。

996
00:42:44.600 --> 00:42:45.980
So he's not going to go with Michael.
所以他不会跟着迈克尔走。

997
00:42:46.240 --> 00:42:48.920
But I'm not sure why Michael doesn't want Dwight.
但我不太确定为什么迈克尔不想让德怀特加入。

998
00:42:49.060 --> 00:42:49.700
Do you have any thoughts?
你有什么想法吗？

999
00:42:50.360 --> 00:42:52.440
You know, that is a really good question.
你知道，这真是个好问题。

1000
00:42:52.720 --> 00:42:55.760
I definitely see why Dwight would say no.
我完全明白为什么德怀特会拒绝。

1001
00:42:56.000 --> 00:42:59.240
But why Michael doesn't ask, I'm not quite sure.
但迈克尔为什么不问，我也不太确定。

1002
00:42:59.760 --> 00:42:59.880
Yeah.
是啊。

1003
00:43:00.180 --> 00:43:01.200
Do you guys have theories?
你们有什么理论吗？

1004
00:43:01.600 --> 00:43:02.940
Yeah, send us your theories.
没错，把你们的理论发给我们。

1005
00:43:03.240 --> 00:43:04.640
We'll add them to a revisited.
我们会把它们加到重温环节里。

1006
00:43:04.980 --> 00:43:07.040
But Michael is going to ask Oscar.
但迈克尔打算去问奥斯卡。

1007
00:43:07.460 --> 00:43:10.780
And the way he's going to do that is by putting a note in his sandwich.
他打算把纸条塞进奥斯卡的午餐三明治里。

1008
00:43:10.780 --> 00:43:12.860
A piece of paper that he bites into.
一张他咬下去会吃到的纸条。

1009
00:43:13.060 --> 00:43:14.260
Don't worry, it's sterile.
别担心，那是消毒过的。

1010
00:43:14.760 --> 00:43:16.800
Just saying sterile doesn't mean it's sterile.
光说消毒过可不代表它真的消毒过。

1011
00:43:16.940 --> 00:43:17.920
I loved that line.
我喜欢这句台词。

1012
00:43:18.120 --> 00:43:22.160
It's like just saying bankrupt doesn't mean he declared bankruptcy.
就像光说破产并不代表他真的申请了破产一样。

1013
00:43:22.480 --> 00:43:22.960
Exactly.
没错。

1014
00:43:24.200 --> 00:43:26.400
Michael gets Oscar to meet him outside.
迈克尔让奥斯卡到外面去见他。

1015
00:43:26.800 --> 00:43:34.560
And Oscar immediately starts offering very practical advice about how most new businesses don't turn a profit for the first two years.
奥斯卡立刻开始提供非常实用的建议，说大多数新企业头两年都不会盈利。

1016
00:43:35.200 --> 00:43:37.580
And, you know, can he afford that?
而且，你知道，他负担得起吗？

1017
00:43:37.740 --> 00:43:40.160
Can he afford to make no money for two years?
他负担得起两年不赚钱吗？

1018
00:43:40.600 --> 00:43:40.840
Right.
对。

1019
00:43:41.140 --> 00:43:43.460
Well, Michael's like, hey, hey, stop convincing me.
迈克尔就说，嘿，嘿，别再劝我了。

1020
00:43:43.540 --> 00:43:44.640
You got the job.
你被录用了。

1021
00:43:45.640 --> 00:43:47.620
With all your number lingo.
就凭你那一套数字术语。

1022
00:43:48.320 --> 00:43:50.420
But ultimately, Oscar's a no.
但最终，奥斯卡拒绝了。

1023
00:43:50.720 --> 00:43:56.060
And that means that he has to move on to Stanley, who he's going to stalk outside the bathroom.
这意味着他必须去找斯坦利，他打算在洗手间外面跟踪他。

1024
00:43:56.380 --> 00:43:56.820
Outside?
外面？

1025
00:43:57.160 --> 00:43:58.100
He's inside.
他在里面。

1026
00:43:58.100 --> 00:43:59.620
I guess outside the stall.
我想是在隔间外面。

1027
00:44:00.020 --> 00:44:04.660
I don't know how urinals work, but I imagine he walked up while he was just peeing.
我不知道小便池是怎么用的，但我猜他是在他小便的时候走过去的。

1028
00:44:04.660 --> 00:44:06.960
Because Stanley's like, I'm urinating.
因为斯坦利说，我正在小便。

1029
00:44:07.480 --> 00:44:08.740
Michael keeps talking to him.
迈克尔还在不停地跟他说话。

1030
00:44:08.860 --> 00:44:09.660
Stanley's like, no.
斯坦利说，不行。

1031
00:44:10.420 --> 00:44:13.420
Michael has then a very sad talking head where he's like, you know what?
迈克尔随后有一个非常悲伤的单人采访，他说，你知道吗？

1032
00:44:13.520 --> 00:44:16.000
No one said yes to prom, but I still had a good time.
没人答应跟我去舞会，但我还是玩得很开心。

1033
00:44:16.720 --> 00:44:17.420
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1034
00:44:17.700 --> 00:44:17.940
What?
什么？

1035
00:44:19.220 --> 00:44:20.500
Pam fixed the copier.
帕姆修好了复印机。

1036
00:44:20.680 --> 00:44:23.000
After four hours, she did it.
花了四个小时，她做到了。

1037
00:44:23.120 --> 00:44:24.020
She didn't let it beat her.
她没有被它打败。

1038
00:44:24.360 --> 00:44:25.300
No, she did not.
不，她没有。

1039
00:44:25.440 --> 00:44:27.520
She knows everything about this machine.
她对这台机器了如指掌。

1040
00:44:28.060 --> 00:44:29.900
Phyllis is going to copy a piece of paper.
菲利斯要去复印一张纸。

1041
00:44:30.280 --> 00:44:32.160
And Pam is like, did it work?
帕姆就问，成功了吗？

1042
00:44:32.400 --> 00:44:33.300
How is it?
怎么样？

1043
00:44:33.300 --> 00:44:35.360
And Phyllis is like, fine.
菲利斯说，挺好的。

1044
00:44:36.200 --> 00:44:36.960
Fine.
挺好的。

1045
00:44:37.420 --> 00:44:41.200
So this whole copier storyline felt very familiar to me.
所以整个复印机的故事线让我觉得非常熟悉。

1046
00:44:41.400 --> 00:44:49.520
Having worked many temp jobs, having fixed many copiers in my real life, and it just felt
因为我做过很多临时工，在现实生活中修过很多复印机，这感觉

1047
00:44:49.520 --> 00:44:54.560
to me like it was written by someone who also had this personal knowledge.
就像是出自一个同样有这种亲身经历的人之手。

1048
00:44:54.960 --> 00:44:55.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1049
00:44:55.720 --> 00:44:59.980
So I had to ask Aaron, have you had experience with copiers?
所以我不得不问亚伦，你有过修理复印机的经历吗？

1050
00:44:59.980 --> 00:45:04.700
You know, because so many of his real life stories have wound up in our scripts, like
你知道，因为他现实生活中的很多故事最终都写进了我们的剧本里，比如

1051
00:45:04.700 --> 00:45:06.340
running past the speed meter.
跑过了测速仪。

1052
00:45:06.620 --> 00:45:06.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1053
00:45:06.920 --> 00:45:09.260
And this whole copier story has so many details.
而且整个复印机的故事里有太多的细节了。

1054
00:45:09.680 --> 00:45:13.000
So as it turns out, yes, yes.
结果证明，是的，没错。

1055
00:45:13.080 --> 00:45:17.620
He told us that he temped in a ton of offices when he was a struggling standup in New York,
他告诉我们，当他在纽约努力做单口喜剧演员时，他在很多办公室做过临时工，

1056
00:45:17.620 --> 00:45:23.420
and he quickly learned that if you could unjam the copier, you held the power.
他很快就发现，如果你能修好卡纸的复印机，你就掌握了权力。

1057
00:45:24.060 --> 00:45:24.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1058
00:45:24.720 --> 00:45:26.780
He actually said, quote,
他实际上是这么说的，引用一下，

1059
00:45:33.600 --> 00:45:40.360
And only a person who has done the copier thing, I feel like, totally gets it, so I totally
我觉得只有做过复印机工作的人才能完全理解，所以我完全

1060
00:45:40.360 --> 00:45:40.860
get it.
理解。

1061
00:45:41.320 --> 00:45:47.180
He said that he would actually copy the user manuals and take them home and read them over
他说他甚至会把用户手册复印下来带回家，在周末

1062
00:45:47.180 --> 00:45:47.500
the week.
读完。

1063
00:45:47.620 --> 00:45:50.000
That's the part that really got me.
那部分真的触动了我。

1064
00:45:50.180 --> 00:45:53.080
He would, like, learn everything from the manual.
他会从手册里学习一切。

1065
00:45:53.560 --> 00:45:54.820
Aaron, I feel you.
亚伦，我懂你。

1066
00:45:54.820 --> 00:45:58.960
Thank you for writing this runner for Pam, because I was able to draw on a lot of my real
谢谢你为帕姆写了这个贯穿始终的梗，因为我在表演这个复印机故事时，

1067
00:45:58.960 --> 00:46:02.840
life experience when it came to performing this copier story.
能够借鉴我生活中很多真实的经历。

1068
00:46:03.320 --> 00:46:04.200
Well, I don't know.
嗯，我不知道。

1069
00:46:04.280 --> 00:46:08.340
Did Michael leave the fakie order form in the copier?
迈克尔把那张假订单留在复印机里了吗？

1070
00:46:08.500 --> 00:46:09.540
Charles finds it.
查尔斯发现了它。

1071
00:46:09.680 --> 00:46:10.520
How does he find it?
他是怎么发现的？

1072
00:46:10.540 --> 00:46:11.280
We don't know.
我们不知道。

1073
00:46:11.400 --> 00:46:15.660
But he's going to get Hank, and they're going to escort him out the building.
但他会去找汉克，他们会把他护送出大楼。

1074
00:46:16.620 --> 00:46:17.580
I am sorry.
我很抱歉。

1075
00:46:17.580 --> 00:46:25.040
I am not sure that there is a recurring character that I love more than Hugh Dane as Hank.
我不确定还有哪个常驻角色比休·丹恩饰演的汉克更让我喜爱。

1076
00:46:25.440 --> 00:46:25.800
I know.
我知道。

1077
00:46:25.960 --> 00:46:27.880
When Michael's like, Hank, come on.
当迈克尔说，汉克，来吧。

1078
00:46:27.980 --> 00:46:29.080
Escort Charles out.
把查尔斯送出去。

1079
00:46:29.200 --> 00:46:30.740
And Hank's like, come on, man.
而汉克说，得了吧，伙计。

1080
00:46:30.820 --> 00:46:31.320
I know.
我知道。

1081
00:46:31.440 --> 00:46:32.080
Just come on.
就过来吧。

1082
00:46:33.760 --> 00:46:34.980
He's so good.
他演得太好了。

1083
00:46:35.320 --> 00:46:36.080
So good.
太棒了。

1084
00:46:36.560 --> 00:46:38.740
Michael really wanted to make a farewell speech.
迈克尔真的很想发表告别演说。

1085
00:46:38.880 --> 00:46:40.500
Charles is not going to have that.
查尔斯可不会让他如愿。

1086
00:46:40.500 --> 00:46:47.420
And everyone watches him as he leaves, and he's like yelling things from his car, right?
大家看着他离开，他在车里大喊大叫，对吧？

1087
00:46:47.420 --> 00:46:50.980
He's yelling from the parking lot, and everyone's looking down, and they're like, what's he
他在停车场大喊，大家都在往下看，他们说，他在

1088
00:46:50.980 --> 00:46:51.340
saying?
说什么？

1089
00:46:51.340 --> 00:46:52.640
We can't hear what he's saying.
我们听不清他在说什么。

1090
00:46:52.900 --> 00:46:54.580
This is what it said in the script.
剧本里是这么写的。

1091
00:46:54.820 --> 00:46:55.280
All right.
好吧。

1092
00:46:55.840 --> 00:46:57.380
Michael walks toward his car.
迈克尔走向他的车。

1093
00:46:57.760 --> 00:47:00.020
Everybody watches from the conference room above.
大家从上面的会议室看着他。

1094
00:47:00.340 --> 00:47:03.860
Michael stops at his car and looks up at the Dunder Mifflin windows.
迈克尔在车旁停下，抬头看向邓德·米夫林的窗户。

1095
00:47:04.460 --> 00:47:06.160
And then he yells this.
然后他大喊了这一句。

1096
00:47:06.660 --> 00:47:07.540
This is it.
就是这个。

1097
00:47:07.700 --> 00:47:08.600
This is goodbye.
这就是告别。

1098
00:47:08.920 --> 00:47:09.400
Forever.
永远的。

1099
00:47:09.900 --> 00:47:10.240
Ah!
啊！

1100
00:47:10.900 --> 00:47:12.480
It's such a nice day out here.
外面天气真好。

1101
00:47:12.760 --> 00:47:13.320
Freedom!
自由！

1102
00:47:26.120 --> 00:47:27.940
That is what was in the script.
剧本里就是这么写的。

1103
00:47:28.140 --> 00:47:31.400
And then it says he screeches his tires and drives off.
然后写着他尖叫着踩下油门开车离开。

1104
00:47:31.540 --> 00:47:33.020
The camera follows his car.
镜头跟着他的车。

1105
