00:54:33.460 --> 00:54:34.560
I'll bring your stuff home.
我会把你东西带回家的。

1259
00:54:35.060 --> 00:54:38.100
So he did address it, but it ended up getting cut.
所以他确实处理了这件事，但最终还是被剪掉了。

1260
00:54:38.300 --> 00:54:39.880
I think it was the right move to cut it.
我觉得剪掉是正确的做法。

1261
00:54:39.980 --> 00:54:44.480
Because it seems like, I don't know, a real thing Pam is holding onto that I don't think
因为这看起来像是帕姆心里一直有个疙瘩，但我并不觉得她有。

1262
00:54:44.480 --> 00:54:45.000
she is.
不，我不这么认为。

1263
00:54:45.120 --> 00:54:46.100
No, I don't think so.
吉姆一给她看那房子，她就喜欢上了。

1264
00:54:46.220 --> 00:54:49.380
As soon as Jim showed her the house, she loved it.
她感受到了关爱和被爱。

1265
00:54:49.520 --> 00:54:51.020
She felt cared for and loved.
她接受了这一切，我觉得从那以后她一直很幸福。

1266
00:54:51.020 --> 00:54:54.500
She took it on, and I think she's been very happy ever since.
所以我很高兴他们没有把那设定成帕姆心中挥之不去的怨恨。

1267
00:54:54.620 --> 00:54:58.680
So I'm glad that they didn't pin that as some sort of lingering resentment for Pam.
没错。

1268
00:54:58.900 --> 00:54:59.040
Yeah.
帕姆在停车场追上了迈克尔。

1269
00:54:59.820 --> 00:55:02.020
Pam catches up to Michael in the parking lot.
她说她要一起去，但她想当销售员，而不是前台。

1270
00:55:02.140 --> 00:55:09.020
She says she's coming along, but she wants to be a salesman, not a receptioniSt.
吉姆对此感到有些惊讶。

1271
00:55:09.200 --> 00:55:10.920
And Jim's kind of surprised by that.
他心想，哦，好吧。

1272
00:55:11.000 --> 00:55:12.100
He's like, oh, okay.
没错。

1273
00:55:12.780 --> 00:55:13.040
Yeah.
大家又聚在会议室里，看着帕姆和迈克尔走远。

1274
00:55:13.620 --> 00:55:18.020
And everyone is gathered again up in the conference room, and they're looking down as Pam and
当他们走远时，你能看到那种怀疑。

1275
00:55:18.020 --> 00:55:19.120
Michael walk away.
你看到他们的神情从胜利转变为一种怀疑。

1276
00:55:19.680 --> 00:55:24.140
And as they're walking away, you can see the doubt.
嗯，很多人把这个结局比作《毕业生》的结局。

1277
00:55:24.360 --> 00:55:28.480
You see this change of them being from triumphant to kind of doubt.
剧透预警，给那些没看过《毕业生》的人，电影最后，

1278
00:55:29.640 --> 00:55:33.320
Well, a lot of people liken this ending to the ending of The Graduate.
达斯汀·霍夫曼饰演的本杰明闯入了他心爱之人伊莱恩的婚礼，

1279
00:55:34.000 --> 00:55:38.780
And spoiler alert to anyone who's never seen The Graduate, but at the end of the movie,
两人从教堂逃了出来。

1280
00:55:39.060 --> 00:55:44.600
the character of Benjamin, who's played by Dustin Hoffman, crashes the wedding of his
他们一起大笑，然后跳上一辆城市公交车，那一幕总是让人觉得非常激动。

1281
00:55:44.600 --> 00:55:48.540
love, Elaine, and the two of them are running away from the church.
他们坐下后，随着坐在那里，他们的表情慢慢发生了变化。

1282
00:55:48.720 --> 00:55:53.700
They're laughing together, and then they jump onto this city bus, and it's always just so
那是非常著名的场景。

1283
00:55:53.700 --> 00:55:54.160
exciting.
太棒了。

1284
00:55:54.320 --> 00:55:58.800
And they take their seat, and while they're sitting there, their expressions kind of slowly
嗯，在剧本里，我们这一幕的舞台指示是这样的。

1285
00:55:58.800 --> 00:55:59.340
change.
吉姆挥手告别迈克尔和帕姆一起离开。

1286
00:55:59.960 --> 00:56:01.300
It's a really famous scene.
镜头停留在他们的脸上，表现他们从幻想回到现实的过程。

1287
00:56:01.420 --> 00:56:02.040
It's so good.
所以拍摄这一幕时我没想过《毕业生》。

1288
00:56:02.040 --> 00:56:07.620
Well, in the script, our stage direction for this scene was this.
我想的是查尔斯·格罗丁主演的电影《心碎度蜜月》里的另一个场景。

1289
00:56:07.900 --> 00:56:11.040
Jim waves as Michael and Pam walk out together.
你看过吗？

1290
00:56:11.460 --> 00:56:16.280
We stay on their faces as they transition from fantasy to reality.
我是说，很久以前看过。

1291
00:56:16.640 --> 00:56:19.720
So I was not thinking of The Graduate when we shot this.
好吧，再次剧透预警，电影最后，他终于娶到了梦中情人西碧尔·谢泼德。

1292
00:56:19.900 --> 00:56:25.460
I was thinking of a different scene from the movie The Heartbreak Kid with Charles Grodin.
他整部电影都在追求她。

1293
00:56:25.880 --> 00:56:27.020
Have you seen it?
他在婚宴上坐在沙发上，然后你就能看到一种倦怠感笼罩在他的脸上。

1294
00:56:27.240 --> 00:56:29.040
I mean, a long time ago.
他心想，接下来该干什么呢？

1295
00:56:29.040 --> 00:56:35.220
Well, again, I guess, spoiler alert, at the end of this movie, he's finally married the
没错。

1296
00:56:35.220 --> 00:56:36.640
woman of his dreams, Sybil Shepard.
没错。

1297
00:56:36.700 --> 00:56:38.140
He's been chasing her through the whole movie.
没错。

1298
00:56:38.820 --> 00:56:46.180
He sits down on the couch at their reception, and then you just see this sort of like malaise
没错。

1299
00:56:46.180 --> 00:56:47.480
wash over his face.
没错。

1300
00:56:47.540 --> 00:56:49.220
And he's like, what now?
没错。

1301
00:56:49.820 --> 00:56:52.860
Because for him, it's all about the joy of the pursuit.
因为对他来说，一切都在于追求过程中的乐趣。

1302
00:56:52.860 --> 00:56:54.480
But now he did it.
但他现在做到了。

1303
00:56:54.960 --> 00:56:57.500
And you can tell he's already restless.
而且看得出来他已经坐不住了。

1304
00:56:57.960 --> 00:57:01.600
I thought of that movie because I always think that's such a perfect moment of acting.
我想到那部电影是因为我一直觉得那是表演中非常完美的一个瞬间。

1305
00:57:01.860 --> 00:57:03.180
I mean, he's so good in that movie.
我是说，他在那部电影里演得太好了。

1306
00:57:03.460 --> 00:57:04.400
But anyway.
但话说回来。

1307
00:57:04.840 --> 00:57:09.800
Well, I will tell you that Tom Cruise and Renee Zellweger in the elevator holding a goldfish
好吧，我得告诉你，汤姆·克鲁斯和蕾妮·齐薇格在电梯里拿着金鱼的那一幕，

1308
00:57:09.800 --> 00:57:11.120
also have a moment like that.
也有过类似的瞬间。

1309
00:57:11.220 --> 00:57:11.560
Hey!
嘿！

1310
00:57:11.560 --> 00:57:13.540
Because I re-watched the movie last night.
因为我昨晚重温了那部电影。

1311
00:57:15.380 --> 00:57:18.900
Well, this episode ends with something I absolutely love.
嗯，这一集结尾的内容我非常喜欢。

1312
00:57:19.020 --> 00:57:20.340
There's a conference room scene.
有一个会议室的场景。

1313
00:57:20.620 --> 00:57:23.080
Charles is telling everyone we've lost some employees.
查尔斯告诉大家我们失去了一些员工。

1314
00:57:23.080 --> 00:57:24.780
We're going to have to do some shifting around.
我们需要进行一些人员调动。

1315
00:57:25.640 --> 00:57:27.380
And this is so great.
这一段太棒了。

1316
00:57:27.520 --> 00:57:29.060
Everyone's reactions are so good.
每个人的反应都非常到位。

1317
00:57:29.200 --> 00:57:30.200
He's like, you know what?
他说，你知道吗？

1318
00:57:30.400 --> 00:57:32.900
Kevin, you're going to be answering phones at reception.
凯文，你要去前台接电话。

1319
00:57:33.180 --> 00:57:35.260
Everyone in the room is like, what?
房间里的每个人都一脸震惊，什么？

1320
00:57:35.540 --> 00:57:36.060
I know.
我知道。

1321
00:57:36.140 --> 00:57:36.940
I know.
我知道。

1322
00:57:37.480 --> 00:57:39.860
I am very much in the foreground of this shot.
我在这个镜头里非常显眼。

1323
00:57:39.860 --> 00:57:43.680
That was on purpose because they wanted me to react, obviously.
那是故意的，因为他们显然希望我做出反应。

1324
00:57:44.300 --> 00:57:49.060
And then he says he's going to put Stanley, who's doing his crossword, barely awake,
然后他说他要让斯坦利——那个正在做填字游戏、几乎还没睡醒的人——

1325
00:57:49.240 --> 00:57:50.740
in charge of productivity.
负责生产力工作。

1326
00:57:51.000 --> 00:57:52.680
Dwight is like, are you kidding me?
德怀特心想，你在开玩笑吗？

1327
00:57:53.140 --> 00:57:57.980
Aaron said he pitched that idea of having Charles put Kevin in charge of the phones,
亚伦说他提议让查尔斯安排凯文去接电话，

1328
00:57:57.980 --> 00:58:02.080
which is going to pay off beautifully in the cold open of next week's episode.
这将在下周剧集的冷开场中产生绝佳的效果。

1329
00:58:02.400 --> 00:58:05.800
But he said it just makes him giggle to think that, like,
但他表示，一想到查尔斯在迈克尔离开后，

1330
00:58:05.800 --> 00:58:10.940
Charles' big power move after Michael leaves is putting Kevin in charge of the phones.
最大的权力举措竟然是让凯文去接电话，他就忍不住发笑。

1331
00:58:11.180 --> 00:58:13.060
Like, he's like, I got this place.
就像是，他觉得，这地方我罩着。

1332
00:58:13.200 --> 00:58:13.620
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

1333
00:58:13.660 --> 00:58:14.660
I know what to do.
我知道该怎么做。

1334
00:58:15.340 --> 00:58:19.960
Speaking of the next episode, ironically, it did not air for two weeks.
说到下一集，讽刺的是，它停播了两周。

1335
00:58:20.400 --> 00:58:21.260
Oh, no way!
哦，不会吧！

1336
00:58:21.400 --> 00:58:22.560
Yes, there was a break.
是的，中间有个间歇。

1337
00:58:22.740 --> 00:58:24.340
I just thought that was really funny.
我只是觉得这真的很有趣。

1338
00:58:24.460 --> 00:58:25.520
People had to really wait.
观众们真的等了很久。

1339
00:58:25.920 --> 00:58:26.440
Two weeks.
两周。

1340
00:58:26.520 --> 00:58:27.880
Yeah, this was a big cliffhanger.
是啊，这可是个巨大的悬念。

1341
00:58:28.920 --> 00:58:33.700
Also, this is the last episode that Pam was a receptionist ever.
另外，这是帕姆作为前台接待员的最后一集。

1342
00:58:33.920 --> 00:58:34.300
Ever?
最后一集？

1343
00:58:34.420 --> 00:58:34.860
In the office.
在办公室里。

1344
00:58:35.280 --> 00:58:35.460
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1345
00:58:35.560 --> 00:58:37.580
She never returns to the receptionist's desk.
她再也没有回到前台接待处。

1346
00:58:37.700 --> 00:58:39.120
Let's finish our scotch and splenda.
让我们喝完我们的苏格兰威士忌加代糖。

1347
00:58:39.540 --> 00:58:41.580
To Pam, our IP receptioniSt.
敬帕姆，我们最棒的前台接待员。

1348
00:58:41.660 --> 00:58:41.960
I know.
我知道。

1349
00:58:42.280 --> 00:58:43.320
Next up, Salesman.
接下来是《推销员》。

1350
00:58:45.120 --> 00:58:46.040
To Pam!
敬帕姆！

1351
00:58:46.860 --> 00:58:48.240
I didn't know that either.
我当时也不知道。

1352
00:58:48.820 --> 00:58:49.120
Wow.
哇。

1353
00:58:49.120 --> 00:58:51.060
When we filmed this episode, I didn't know.
我们拍这一集的时候，我并不知情。

1354
00:58:51.200 --> 00:58:54.080
I didn't know that you didn't know at the time.
我当时都不知道你不知道。

1355
00:58:54.420 --> 00:58:54.820
Yeah.
是啊。

1356
00:58:54.820 --> 00:58:56.440
Well, we didn't know what was going to happen.
嗯，我们当时也不知道会发生什么。

1357
00:58:56.620 --> 00:58:57.060
We didn't.
确实不知道。

1358
00:58:57.960 --> 00:58:58.360
Wow.
哇。

1359
00:58:58.700 --> 00:59:00.660
I should have worn my t-shirt today that says,
我今天本该穿上那件T恤的，上面写着，

1360
